Package: MoFIA
Type: Package
Title: Moderated Factor and Item Analysis
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Henrik", "Godmann", email = "hrgodmann@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Fits moderated nonlinear factor analysis models (Bauer and Hussong,
    2009, <doi:10.1037/a0015583>; Bauer, 2017, <doi:10.1037/met0000077>) by
    marginal maximum likelihood. Item loadings, thresholds or intercepts and
    residual variances, as well as factor means, variances and correlations,
    can depend on any number of moderators. Items can be binary, ordinal (logit
    or probit link), continuous, or mixed. The factors are integrated out by
    adaptive Gauss-Hermite quadrature with analytic gradients in C++. Provides
    maximum likelihood, robust (sandwich) and score-based standard errors,
    scaled likelihood-ratio tests (Satorra and Bentler, 2001,
    <doi:10.1007/BF02296192>) and Wald tests for measurement invariance and
    differential item functioning.
